{{!
	Renders one row of the site footer as a list.

	Called by Footer.mustache, the only consumer, once for each of the three footer
	portlets: data-footer-info, data-footer-places and data-footer-icons. The enclosing
	footer element, its role and the user-language attributes belong to that caller and
	are deliberately not repeated here.

	Every id below, and the row class, are owned by MediaWiki core (SkinComponentFooter
	and SkinComponentMenu) rather than by this skin, and gadgets, user styles, extensions
	and the print stylesheet all select on them. They are therefore passed through
	verbatim, with no notion- prefix and no renaming of any kind. The Notion restyle of
	the footer lives entirely in resources/skins.notion.styles/components/Footer.less,
	which hangs off exactly these core-owned hooks.

	@typedef object footerItem
	@prop string id of list item element, assigned by core, e.g. footer-info-lastmod,
		footer-places-privacy or footer-poweredbyico
	@prop string html of list item: already-rendered core markup containing anchors and,
		in the icons row, image elements, so it is emitted unescaped

	@typedef object footerRow
	@prop string id of list element: footer-info, footer-places or footer-icons
	@prop string|null class of list element, e.g. mw-portlet mw-portlet-footer-info.
		Rendered only when truthy, with the separating space held inside the conditional
		section so that an empty class attribute is never emitted
	@prop footerItem[] array-items the items of this row, in the order core built them

	Deliberate and easy to break: the id expression is context-shadowed. At the top level
	it resolves to the row id, while inside the array-items section the item is pushed
	onto the context stack, so the very same expression resolves to the item id there.
	Both readings are intended; do not hoist, rename or otherwise "correct" either one.

	The list element is unconditional on purpose. The caller only enters this partial for
	a row core actually produced, so a second guard here would add nothing and would risk
	suppressing a row that is legitimately present but empty.

	Two authoring constraints keep this comment inert, and both are easy to undo by accident.
	First, expressions are described in prose because a mustache comment ends at its first
	closing double brace, so an inline example would terminate the comment early and leak the
	remainder into the rendered footer. Second, the comment closes tight against the list
	element below, with no newline between them, because the caller includes this partial in
	the middle of a line: a newline there would be emitted once per footer row. This is the
	same whitespace-swallowing idiom the Button, Link and MenuListItem partials use.
}}<ul id="{{id}}"{{#class}} class="{{.}}"{{/class}}>
	{{#array-items}}
	<li id="{{id}}">{{{html}}}</li>
	{{/array-items}}
</ul>
